    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a bit of a generic answer lol. but looking at the history of tech, like the industrial revolution or even the internet, it always seems like once the genie is out of the bottle, there's no stopping it. even if we try to regulate, the tech just moves faster. isn't it more accurate to say that the technological trajectory is basically fixed and policy is just reacting to it?",
